# REPLACE @OWNER-REPLACE-ME BELOW WITH YOUR OWN GITHUB HANDLE OR TEAM.
#
# Until you do, every rule here is inert: GitHub silently ignores an owner that
# is not a collaborator on this repository, so this file will LOOK like
# governance and enforce nothing. That failure is quiet, which is the reason it
# is called out in the first line rather than the last.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Which paths a human must approve, as data rather than judgement at merge time.
#
# Shape from kubernetes/community's OWNERS: ownership is path-scoped and
# machine-readable, so "may this land unattended" is a lookup, not a decision
# someone makes while tired. GitHub applies the LAST matching pattern, so the
# catch-all goes first and the protected paths override it.
#
# This is the capability layer's starting point, seeded on install and never
# overwritten afterwards. The paths below are the layer's own: they run
# automatically, on every turn, in every repository the layer reaches. Add your
# product's own protected paths beneath them.

*                               @OWNER-REPLACE-ME

# --- runs unattended -----------------------------------------------------------
# A hook fires on its own and its failure mode is silence. A wrong pattern in the
# secret scanner blocks every commit; a wrong branch guard lets one onto main.
/.claude/hooks/                 @OWNER-REPLACE-ME
/.claude/settings.json          @OWNER-REPLACE-ME

# --- decides what "green" means ------------------------------------------------
# Weakening a check is indistinguishable from fixing one, in a diff.
/.claude/project-checks.json    @OWNER-REPLACE-ME
/.github/workflows/             @OWNER-REPLACE-ME
/tools/run_checks.py            @OWNER-REPLACE-ME

# --- the rules themselves ------------------------------------------------------
/.claude/constitution.md        @OWNER-REPLACE-ME
/CLAUDE.md                      @OWNER-REPLACE-ME

# --- least reversible ----------------------------------------------------------
# The pattern is listed so the answer is already written down on the day a
# migration first appears, rather than decided in the PR that adds it.
/migrations/                    @OWNER-REPLACE-ME
**/migrations/                  @OWNER-REPLACE-ME
